      "properties": {},
      "widgets_values": [
        "## Roformer \\u2014 Two-Model Ensemble (the mvsep.com leaderboard move)\n\nThe best mvsep.com results are **ensembles**: several models run on the same song, their stems blended. Two levers do most of the work:\n\n- **Max Spec / Min Spec** (UVR's exact math): per STFT bin, keep the value of the model with the larger / smaller magnitude (phase included). Leaderboard recipe: **max spec for vocals, min spec for the instrumental**.\n- **Exact residual**: instead of trusting a model's predicted instrumental, compute `mix \\u2212 ensemble(vocals)` \\u2014 the split is exact (ensemble + residual == mix).\n\n**This graph**\n1. The mix runs through **two models**: `sw-6stem` (six stems) and `hyperace-v2-voc` (vocals + residual).\n2. **Roformer Ensemble (max spec)** blends the two vocals predictions.\n3. **Roformer Ensemble (invert, mix connected)** blends the two vocals (average) and subtracts them from the original mix \\u2014 the exact-residual instrumental.\n4. Saves: both ensemble stems (native Save Audio) and all six `sw-6stem` stems (Roformer Save Audio).\n\nAdd more models: another Loader + Separate + To Audio into the Ensemble's next audio slot (up to eight). The graph is the saved ensemble \\u2014 every slot and option is in the file.\n\nGPU strongly recommended; `sw-6stem` wants about 10 GB of VRAM."
      ],
      "title": "Roformer \u2014 Two-Model Ensemble"
    },
